== SURF_LEAVE
# LEAVE: text out, counted, each with its closing unit (DELTA10 L1: L0 BOUNDARY, L1-L5 ; DELTA13 D2: L6) — empty
# until the module exists ; a row matching no failing position fails STALE
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-2a (DELTA14 F2, DELTA15 C1.3): L7 `key_text`, a NewKey's text where it meets a text operation outside the
# module (one site at DK1-2a: struct_arm.rs:113, deleted by DK1-4b) ; the bridge closes at DK3-b
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-2d (2026-11-24): bridge w11 closed: L8 (DK1-2b's two TEXT doors of SlotKey's sealed half, `slot_text` / `slot_owned`) closed with it, its two rows deleted
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-3 (2026-11-24): the read side: L9 `at_text`, an AtKey's text where it meets a text operation outside the module — held.rs clk_refused_at's
# compare with the walk's text key (DK1-4b types the walk), ports.rs elaborate_virtual_iface's two member-key glues (DK1-5a, key_in: closed there)
# and bind_iface_port's X15 prefix (DK3-a): the bridge closes with its last row, DK3-a
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-4a (2026-11-24): the walk moves in with its text signatures kept (R-G15): L10, the walk's text — the found key (RET Option<String>) and the text its `hit` callback is handed (CB:hit.0 &str), one row per entry (4 + 4) ; each closes at DK1-4b (the walk returns DeclKey, `hit: impl Fn(&AtKey)`)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-4b-1 (2026-11-24): L10's four `CB:hit.0 &str` rows closed (`hit` is handed an `&AtKey`: SURF_ROWS PASS REF, open until DK2) ; its four `RET Option<String>` rows re-dated DK1-4b -> DK1-4b-2 (the found key's type, DELTA16 R-H1)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-4b-2 (2026-11-24): L10 CLOSED — its four `RET Option<String>` rows deleted (the walk returns a DeclKey: SURF_ROWS CARD) ; L11 `found_text`, a found key's text where it meets a text operation outside the module (R-H5: ports.rs bind_iface_port's prefix glue -> DK3-a ; gen_scope_name.rs key_spells_indexed_singleton, frames_static_init.rs frame_init_name_is_local_or_const -> DK3-b, HBR's three rows), deleting unit DK3-b
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-5a (2026-11-25): L5 and L6 CLOSED, rows deleted (Scopes::key_under returns an AtKey ; Scopes::scope_text is private, its last reader outside, hier_resolve, moved in) ; L9 at_text outside 3 -> 1 (ports.rs elaborate_virtual_iface's two member-key glues: src `key_in`, dst `new_key` ; bind_iface_port's X15 prefix left, DK3-a) ; L12 OPENED: Elaborator::indexed_gen_singleton RET Option<String>, the label key `level.label` of a singleton generate scope, read by key_spells_indexed_singleton (gen_scope_name.rs, HBR 1 row), deleting unit DK3-b (it becomes a lexscope entry there and indexed_gen_singleton goes private, DELTA17 F3.1)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-5b (2026-11-25): L1 CLOSED (Scopes::cur_prefix_text private: its last readers outside, names_with_pkg_var_aliases and elaborate_package's snapshot argument, moved in or gone) and L7 CLOSED at DK1-5b, not DK3-b (key_text pub(super): elaborate_package hands its six key lists to decl_keep_snapshot as `&NewKey`s) — both rows deleted ; L13 OPENED: Elaborator::names_with_pkg_var_aliases RET std::collections::BTreeSet<String>, the bare names a package variable import binds in the current scope with the names handed in, read by its four callers outside (block_local_feed.rs, iface_inst.rs, instance.rs x2), deleting unit DK3-a (DELTA18 T7: L13's closing form is decided there, R-I3)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK3-a (2026-11-26): L4 CLOSED (display_of_key_text private: its one caller, net_name_table, moved in and returns Vec<Shown>) and L9 CLOSED (at_text deleted: its last reader, bind_iface_port's X15 prefix, is alias_iface_port's `at_cur(..).0` inside) — two rows deleted ; L13 is PERMANENT (ruling R-K3, q6: the bare declared names of the current scope leave as text) and gains bare_name_of_net (X12, dynarr.rs's snapshot holder: its bare name)
# NOT-PROMISED NP19-7 (§5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK3-a): scope_home's LEAVE_PERMANENT reads this table's id column only — a row given id L13 (or L0) with closes `permanent` passes it (scope_home.tables HBR's head)
# NOT-PROMISED NP19-9 / NP19-10 / NP19-11 (§5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK3-b): a `Deref` impl written back on a store, a text entry widened to `pub(crate)` and a `pub(crate)` entry respelled `pub` all compile ; the first two are this table's rows (IMPL-TRAIT, NEW ROW), the third no rule's (scope_home.tables HBR's head)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK3-b (2026-11-27): L11 CLOSED (found_text pub(super): its last reader outside, frame_init_name_is_local_or_const, reads DeclKey::has_func_segment) and L12 CLOSED (indexed_gen_singleton private, -> bool ; key_spells_indexed_singleton moved in) — two rows deleted
id	item	position	type	closes
