== SURF_ENTER
# ENTER: text or a number in (IN-TOTAL, DELTA12 S2), by role (to-scope / to-display / lookup /
# carried / index) and what the position holds (the kind and IN-TOTAL's path ; a moved path FAILS)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-4a (2026-11-24): the walk entries' `name` (the bare name the walk composes each key from) and is_gen_scope_segment's `seg` (a segment of a scope text it asks one question of) — lookup
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-4b-1 (2026-11-24): is_gen_scope_segment is pub(super) (walk.rs's own question, off the surface): its `seg` row deleted
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-4b-2 (2026-11-24): Scopes::gen_binding_encloses takes the walk's found key (`&DeclKey`): its `key` row deleted (no text in)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-5a (2026-11-25): hier_resolve `path` (the dotted path the resolver composes keys from) and `table` (the caller's text-keyed leaf map, window w9: retyped at DK3-b, DELTA18 T4) ; indexed_gen_singleton `level` / `seg` (the scope text and the source segment its label key is formed from) ; key_in `member` (an interface member's name) — lookup
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-5b (2026-11-25): names_with_pkg_var_aliases `names` (the scope's own declared names, copied into the set it returns) — lookup (`carried` is refused: the body reads it, `.clone()`)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK2 (2026-11-26, form (c)): the four walks are private: their `name` rows gone ; the 23 named entries' `name` (lookup, TEXT str) rows added by the pass
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK3-a (2026-11-26): display_of_key_text's `key` row deleted (private, off the surface) ; + the three by-id entries' `net_id` (the id looked up among symbols' values, NUMBER) and alias_iface_port's `pname` (the port name the alias keys are formed under at the current scope) and `input_of` (the modport's member names, looked up) — lookup
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK3-b (2026-11-27): hier_resolve `table` is `&Keyed<V>` (no text position) ; indexed_gen_singleton private (off the surface) — three rows deleted ; + key_spells_indexed_singleton `user_segs` (the count of the user's segments the scan starts after: index)
