== SURF_E
# E: the Elaborator-taking fns, OUT-F / OUT-C / OUT-M by (fn, name, count) ; FLOW (hand) in /
# payload / text:<sink> (BODY moved to SURF_BODY: BODY-ALL, DELTA11 R2)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-6 (2026-11-25): E3 checks every `text:` flow, per `+` part: `LEAVE-<id>` must be a SURF_LEAVE id (a dangling tag FAILS FLOW ; any non-empty tag passed before) ; any other part is `error`, a SURF_OUT_TYPES entry or a SURF_VOCAB name an entry spells (`DeclKey` in `Option<DeclKey>`)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-4a (2026-11-24): the 7 moved Elaborator fns' rows (is_gen_scope_segment takes no Elaborator) ; flow text:LEAVE-L10 = an op that forms or hands the key text leaving through L10 ; walk_hits_decl_pos' `.walk_scopes_key` is a module call now (row gone)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-4b-1 (2026-11-24): the walk's candidate is an AtKey — `AtKey` OUT-C rows (scoped_key_at_or_above: formed from the text that leaves through L10 RET ; _from / _inner: the empty scratch, as String::new) ; the store probes `.contains_at` ; `hit` is handed an AtKey, no text: its three rows' flow text:LEAVE-L10 -> in
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-4b-2 (2026-11-24): the walk returns a DeclKey — `DeclKey` OUT-C rows (scoped_key_at_or_above, walk_out_from, walk_scopes_key_inner: the scratch moved into the found key) ; walk_hits_decl_pos reads the found key through found_text (`.as_ref` + `.map` for `.as_deref`) ; L10 is deleted: the nine flows text:LEAVE-L10 -> text:DeclKey (the text these ops form leaves in the found key, whose text leaves the module only through L11)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-5a (2026-11-25): the five moved fns' rows (lexscope/hier.rs ; is_hier_scope private, its own rows, R-J7 d: a call to an in-module fn is no OUT-C row, so no `.is_hier_scope` row exists) ; flow `in` but hier_resolve's `.cloned` (payload: the table's value) and indexed_gen_singleton's label key (text:LEAVE-L12) ; `Self::gen_seg_label = 1` (indexed_gen_singleton) is the ONE call from these bodies to a fn outside the module with a text argument: its own IN `seg` passed through, flow `in` (R-J7 a) — NOT pinned by class until DK1-6 (SURF_OUTCALL, R-J7 c): this row is change detection only ; §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-6 (2026-11-25): the class pin is SURF_OUTCALL's row `Elaborator::indexed_gen_singleton · Elaborator::gen_seg_label · 1 · in` (E2: gen_seg_label takes `&str`, so `none` is refused ; the row's `in` is hand, NOT-PROMISED: no data flow) ; this OUT-C row stays change detection
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-5b (2026-11-25): names_with_pkg_var_aliases' rows (moved to lexscope/elab.rs): flow text:LEAVE-L13 where the op forms or hands the text of the set it returns (the two `.clone`s of `names`, the alias keys' `.keys`, the `.rsplit_once` / `.as_str` that cut the bare name, `.to_string`, `.insert`), `in` for the bool tests and the store read ; it calls no fn outside the module (move_census calls_outside=0)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK2 (2026-11-26, form (c)): the 23 named entries' FN / OUT-F / OUT-C rows, flow `in` (the walk's candidate AtKey, read by each store's `contains_at` or by a lane) ; the four walks' rows stand ; a site's closure rows leave with the closure
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK3-a (2026-11-26): + net_key_shown, net_name_table (moved in), net_is_compiler_internal (moved in), bare_name_of_net, alias_iface_port: 5 fns, 51 rows, FLOW read off each body (text:Shown for what net_key_shown / net_name_table hand out, text:LEAVE-L13 for bare_name_of_net's name, in for the rest) ; display_of's four `text:Shown+LEAVE-L4` -> `text:Shown` (L4 closed: its one reader is net_name_table, inside)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK3-b (2026-11-27): the window's in-module calls are the text entries' (a renamed call keeps its old name's FLOW: 16 rows) ; key_spells_indexed_singleton moved in (6 rows, `in`: it answers a bool) ; indexed_gen_singleton private -> bool, its `text:LEAVE-L12` rows `in` (2, L12 closed) ; the stores' OUT-F rows stand: a field whose type names Keyed / KeyedSet is counted (STORE_TYPES, round 2 ; round 1's E1 had dropped the seven KeyedSet rows, four of them text reads no other row named)
