== SURF_OUTCALL
# OUTCALL (§5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-6, 2026-11-25 ; DELTA18 G2.4 E1-E3, R-J3, as corrected by R-J7 (a)): every call from a fn of the module's
# file set to a fn of the crate defined OUTSIDE it, by (item, callee) with a count ; a call with no row or a moved count FAILS OUTCALL,
# a row with no call is STALE. Styles: SELF `self.f` / `(*self).f` / `Self::f` / `<Self>::f` in impl Elaborator, `Elaborator::f` /
# `<Elaborator<'_>>::f` (callee `Elaborator::f`) ; RECV `<expr>.f(..)` on another receiver, resolved by the NAME f against every method
# with a receiver defined outside the file set (callee `.f` ; every definition by that name is read for the class) ; FREE `f(..)` /
# `crate::..::f` / `super::..::f` out of the module / `T::f` of a crate type or trait, `<T as Tr>::f` (callee `f` / `T::f`).
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-6 round 2 (2026-11-25, W/scopebind/dk1_6/r2/claims.tsv): a fn named as a value (`.map(Self::f)`, `let g = f;`,
# `(Self::f)(..)`) counts as a call ; a path's first segment that a `use` of the file binds into the crate is read through it
# (`use crate::m; m::f`, `use crate::Elaborator as El; El::f`, a crate module named like a module of the file set, a bare `f` imported
# over the file set's own private `f`) ; `crate::..::T::f` is outside even when the file set has a type T ; `matches!(e, pat if g)`'s
# e and g and `vec![e; n]` are read (FIX NO17-NO23 ; NO28 shows a closure's body was read already).
# class (E2), computed-constrained from the callee's signature: a parameter spelling a text type (`&str`, `String`, `&String`, `&[&str]`,
# `Vec<String>`, `Option<String>`, `Cow<str>`, `Box<str>`, `impl AsRef<str>`, `impl Into<String>`, a String-keyed map ..), a byte sequence
# (`&[u8]`, `Vec<u8>`), `impl Display` / `impl ToString`, a type parameter so bound (`S: AsRef<str>`, `where S: Into<String>`), or the
# receiver of an impl for str / String (`impl StrExt for str`) takes text (FIX NO24-NO27, NO29) ; none -> `none` ; one or more -> `in` (an
# entered parameter passed through), `error` (the callee is on SURF_OUTCALL_SINKS) or `text:<Lid>` (E3: a SURF_LEAVE row of the
# calling item at position `OUT:<callee>`, type = the callee's text parameters, closes = this row's closes) — never `none`.
# closes: `-` = no closing unit dated (a standing call) ; a text:<Lid> row's is its LEAVE row's.
# On this tree (c5d985ca re-measured, W/scopebind/dk1_6/outcalls.tsv ; round 2's wider reading re-measured: the same 8 rows): SELF 7,
# RECV 1, FREE 2 = 10 calls, 8 rows ; no `text:<Lid>` row.
# gen_seg_label's row is the class pin DK1-5a's OUT-C comment named for DK1-6 (`in`: indexed_gen_singleton's own IN `seg` passed through).
# NOT-PROMISED (what OUTCALL cannot see ; one shape a line, each measured in W/scopebind/dk1_6/r2/claims.tsv):
#  N1  `Self::f(&format!("{k}.x"))` pinned `in`: whether an `in` argument is the entered text or text formed in the module (a syn reader has no data flow).
#  N2  `in` on a calling item with no entered text parameter (`fn outward(&mut self)` passing a literal): `in` is not checked against the caller's parameters.
#  N3  `(w.on_key)(k)`, `f(k)` with `f: impl Fn(&str)`: a fn held in a field or passed in as a parameter — no fn item of the crate is named in the module.
#  N4  `x.get(k)` / `x.is_empty()` on another receiver with the name on SURF_OUTCALL_BLIND (why `std`: on this tree 1 name, is_empty, 41 calls ; why
#      `module`: a method name the file set defines, 0 rows on this tree): the name is not resolved.
#  N5  `self.hier_params.contains_text(..)` / `self.wide_param_bits.range_text(..)` reaching the store through `Deref for Bound<..>` (hier.rs x4, since DK3-b's text entries) and `a != DeclPhase::Win` (`PartialEq::ne`,
#      walk.rs x1): operator and auto-deref trait calls have no call syntax (none takes text on this tree).
#  N6  `x.clone()` / `a == b` on an outside type whose impl is `#[derive(..)]`: a derived method is no fn of the source ; a RECV call reaching a
#      hand-written impl is read by NAME (every outside method so named), never as the one impl the receiver's type picks.
#  N7  `zn! { fn x() { crate::f(k) } }`: a macro's tokens that are no expression list, no `matches!` form, no `vec![e; n]` and begin with no
#      expression (a macro body ; a `macro_rules!` definition's body).
#  N8  `crate::f(k)` with f made by an item macro (`mk_fn!(f)`) or defined in an impl inside `const _: () = { .. }`: the index reads items, not
#      macro output nor items inside a body.
#  N9  `type A = crate::Win; A::f(w, k)` (a `type` alias of an outside type) and `self::super::f(k)` (`self::` is read as the module): an alias
#      or a path spelling the reader does not follow.
#  N10 `crate::f(Holder { s })`, `crate::f(ident)` with `dep::Ident`: a parameter whose struct type HOLDS text is no text parameter (fields are
#      not followed) — the row's class reads `none`.
#  N11 `crate::Wrap(k.to_string())`: a tuple-struct or variant constructor of an outside type is no fn.
#  N12 `self.sink.m(k)`, `hdl_ast::Span::new(..)`, `diag::..`: a call into another crate (the index is this crate's src).
#  N13 a deliberate wrapper that hides the callee: a module fn that forwards to the outside fn (its own call is the row, in the wrapper).
#  N14 `type StrMap = BTreeMap<String, u32>; crate::f(m)` with `m: &StrMap`, or `&Keyed<V>`: a parameter whose text type sits behind a
#      `type` alias or a wrapper type is no text parameter (aliases are not followed) — the row's class reads `none`.
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK2 (2026-11-26, form (c)): each named entry whose closure calls a lane calls it out of the file set (13 `hit_*` lanes of bound/read.rs and held.rs hit_clk_refused), SELF x1, every callee `(&self, k: &AtKey) -> bool`: class none (DELTA19B P50) ; self 7 -> 21, rows 8 -> 22
item	callee	count	class	closes
