== SURF_OUTCALL_BLIND
# OUTCALL's blind list (§5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-6): a method name both a std type and a fn defined outside the file set carry — a call
# `<expr>.<name>(..)` on a receiver other than the Elaborator's `self` is NOT resolved (syntax does not know the receiver's type) ;
# why `std` (the name is on scope_surface.rs's STD_METHODS) or `module` (the file set defines a method by that name) ; a row no call
# uses is STALE (it blinds no call: no method call on another receiver names it while an outside method has that name). On this tree:
# 1 name, `is_empty` why `std` (44 calls since DK3-b: + the two has_no_key bodies, - names_with_pkg_var_aliases' `pkg_var_aliases.is_empty()` (has_no_key) ; 43 since DK3-a: + net_name_table's two, moved in ; ConstFrame::is_empty bound/frame.rs, ReadMark::is_empty read_set.rs are the outside
# definitions) ; 0 rows why `module`. Each row is a NOT-PROMISED shape of SURF_OUTCALL (N4): a call by that name on another receiver
# is not resolved, whatever its receiver's type (round 2: `(*self).name(..)` is the Elaborator's self, SELF, not blinded: FIX NO18). S7-J2's census (modcalls.py, any `fn` name) printed 66 / 69 std-name calls over is_empty, push, contains,
# join: push / contains / join are FREE fns outside (decl_collide.rs, block_local_class.rs, da/expr_effect.rs), which no method call
# can reach, so OUTCALL does not list them.
name	why
is_empty	std
== SURF_OUTCALL_SINKS
# OUTCALL's error sinks (§5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-6): the closed list of callees whose text parameter is a diagnostic's display text, not a
# key (driver.rs Elaborator::error, Elaborator::error_at) — class `error` is admitted only for these ; a row naming no Elaborator fn
# outside the file set with a text parameter is STALE.
callee
Elaborator::error
Elaborator::error_at
