== SURF_CB
# CB (DELTA11 R2): a callback parameter of a surface item, kind Fn | FnMut | FnOnce | fn, its
# argument types, CALLS (hand): once (FnOnce) | per:<what> | probe:<what>. First rows at LS2a.
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-4a (2026-11-24): the four walk entries' `hit`, called once per scope level the walk visits
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-4b-1 (2026-11-24): the four walk entries' `hit` takes the candidate as an `&AtKey` (`hit.0`: PASS REF, open until DK2)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK2 (2026-11-26, form (c)): the four walks are private (off the surface): their four rows gone ; walk_rtn_scopes' stays (outside the claim, L-listed)
item	param	kind	args	calls
Elaborator::with_scope	f	FnOnce	&mut Self	once
== SURF_BODY
# BODY-ALL (DELTA11 R2, R4 N-5): the sha256 of the body tokens of every fn of the file set.
# First rows at LS2a ; each unit's verify prints the rows that changed.
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-4a (2026-11-24): the 8 moved bodies (walk.rs)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-4b-1 (2026-11-24): the walk's six bodies that form or probe the candidate (walk.rs, elab.rs walk_hits_decl_pos) ; at_same (key.rs)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-4b-2 (2026-11-24): the walk returns a DeclKey — scoped_key_at_or_above, walk_scopes_key_inner, walk_out_from (walk.rs), walk_hits_decl_pos (elab.rs), gen_binding_encloses (mod.rs), fb_gen_binding_encloses (tests.rs) ; new: the five `_found` entries, found_text, key_same, DeclKey::is_formed_as / is_formed_at (key.rs)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-5a (2026-11-25): the five moved bodies (lexscope/hier.rs), key_in (key.rs) new ; Scopes::key_under (mod.rs, AtKey) and fb_key_under_and_scope_debug (tests.rs, at_text) changed
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-5b (2026-11-25): names_with_pkg_var_aliases (moved, lexscope/elab.rs) and Scopes::keys_under_cur (lexscope/mod.rs) new ; the order pin fb_keys_under_cur_orders_and_dedups (lexscope/tests.rs) new
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-5b round 2 (2026-11-25, the cost trip on the package path): Scopes::keys_under_cur re-pinned (its key list by value, sorted / deduped / filtered in place, no format!) and the order pin re-pinned (its two calls hand the Vec by value)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK2 (2026-11-26): the 23 named entries' bodies re-pinned for form k6, the best measured inline form, left on T at the cost STOP (W/scopebind/dk2/REPORT.txt): each closure `#[inline(always)] |k|` ; the four walks `#[inline(always)]`, walk_scopes_key_inner / walk_out_from / decl_probe_key `#[inline(always)]`)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK3-b (2026-11-27): the four Deref / DerefMut bodies gone (window deleted) ; the text / q8 entries, has_func_segment and key_spells_indexed_singleton new ; the bodies that call them re-pinned
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK3-b (2026-11-27): the stores are not `Clone` ; the whole-store copy is `snapshot` (Keyed, KeyedSet: RET Self, PASS)
