== SURF_INTERIOR
# INTERIOR (LS1 part 6): the exemptions, each a counted, named row (as LEAVE / ENTER are):
# item, position, the path of names INTERIOR follows to the carrier, why (hand). A row whose
# path moved FAILS INTERIOR ; a row matching no position is STALE. Empty.
item	position	reaches	why
Elaborator::with_scope	IN:f	Self = Elaborator -> Elaborator.const_call_fn -> RefCell	the receiver lent to its callback
== SURF_PLAN
# SURF-PLAN: the 30 fns of plan10/g/moved.tsv (DELTA10 L2), judged by I-SURF on today's signature
# (vis, tier, the normalised signature, verdict, the failing positions, the text IN parameters) ;
# + report_at (L2's LS3 row, N-a), which moved.tsv does not list: 31 rows. LS1 part 5 (DELTA11
# R2): CARD and CB judge them too, with no list consulted (as LEAVE is not): 16 CARD, 8 CB.
# LS1 part 6: INTERIOR judges them too, no list consulted: 1 row (with_scope's callback lends
# `&mut Self`, the Elaborator, which holds a RefCell: lib.rs:555 const_call_fn). LS1 part 7
# (DELTA12 S2): the last column lists every IN parameter IN-TOTAL makes TEXT or NUMBER, by name
# or by content (ENTER-NEEDED) — push_block_local_init + lo, lhs, rhs ; report_at + span ; and
# the COUNTS line gains enter (those parameters), enter_number and in_unknown (fns with one).
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-3 (2026-11-24): the read side: `fq` (scope.rs) is deleted — its row left: 31 -> 30 fns (fail 27 -> 26, ret_fail 24 -> 23,
# ret_text 21 -> 20, enter 39 -> 38) ; its two roles are lexscope's Scopes::at_cur (AtKey) and Scopes::show_miss (Shown)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-4a (2026-11-24): 6 fns moved to lexscope/walk.rs (scoped_key_at_or_above, walk_scopes_key, _from, _inner, _shadowed, decl_probe_key — private now) ; walk_scopes stays in scope.rs (R-G15)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-4b-1 (2026-11-24): the walk entries' `hit` (and decl_probe_key's scratch) take an AtKey — 7 rows re-judged: CB:hit.0 / ARG:key UNKNOWN(AtKey): plan mode judges with no file-set definitions (report_at's UNKNOWN(ReportedAt) since LS3) ; HT-SURF judges the same positions PASS REF ; walk_scopes' table `&Keyed<T>` (R-G15 (a)) ; callback_text 7 -> 1, mut_text 1 -> 0
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-4b-2 (2026-11-24): the walk entries return a DeclKey — 5 rows re-judged: RET=CARD(Option in Option<DeclKey>) ; RET=UNKNOWN(DeclKey) (plan mode judges with no file-set definitions, as UNKNOWN(AtKey) since DK1-4b-1 ; HT-SURF judges the position CARD) ; ret_text 20 -> 15
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-5a (2026-11-25): hier_resolve, hier_key_within, indexed_gen_singleton, singleton_scope_key moved to lexscope/hier.rs (file column ; singleton_scope_key private now) ; + is_hier_scope (R-J2: the resolver's scope question moves in with it, private ; absent from moved.tsv and from this table before) — 30 -> 31 fns
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK1-5b (2026-11-25): + names_with_pkg_var_aliases (X18, the unit's one mover, lexscope/elab.rs ; absent from moved.tsv and this table before: move_census SURF_PLAN absent=1) — 31 -> 32 fns ; decl_keep_snapshot stays outside (R-J1: no row) and keys_under_cur is a new entry, not a moved fn (no row)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK2 (2026-11-26, form (c)): the four generic walks are private (each site calls a named entry, 23, E-1c) — 4 rows re-judged off the surface (their CB:hit / CB:hit.0 / IN:name / RET verdicts leave with the visibility) ; walk_scopes (scope.rs) deleted, its row gone: 32 -> 31 fns ; the entries take `name: &str` (+ `prefix`) and return Option<DeclKey>, no callback (SURF_ROWS)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK3-a (2026-11-26): net_name_table moved to lexscope/disp.rs and returns Vec<Shown> — its row re-homed and re-judged (unit column DK4 kept: moved.tsv's label)
# §5.2 Q-DECLKEY DK3-b (2026-11-27): hier_resolve `table: &Keyed<V>` (step d) and indexed_gen_singleton private -> bool (L12) re-judged from today's signatures
unit	fn	file	vis	tier	signature	verdict	fails	in_enter
DK1	decl_probe_key	lexscope/walk.rs	-	E	(&self, name: &str, key: &mut AtKey, hit: &impl Fn(&AtKey) -> bool) -> bool	FAIL	ARG:key=UNKNOWN(AtKey); CB:hit=CB(a callback Fn(&AtKey)); CB:hit.0=UNKNOWN(AtKey)	name
DK1	hier_key_within	lexscope/hier.rs	-	E	(&self, base: &str, rest: &[String]) -> Option<String>	FAIL	RET=CARD(Option in Option<String>); RET=TEXT(String)	base,rest
DK1	hier_resolve	lexscope/hier.rs	pub(crate)	E	(&self, prefix: &crate::ScopeRef, path: &[String], table: &Keyed<V>) -> Option<V>	FAIL	RET=CARD(Option in Option<V>)	prefix,path,table
DK1	indexed_gen_singleton	lexscope/hier.rs	-	E	(&self, level: &str, seg: &str) -> bool	PASS	-	level,seg
DK1	is_hier_scope	lexscope/hier.rs	-	E	(&self, base: &str) -> bool	PASS	-	base
DK1	names_with_pkg_var_aliases	lexscope/elab.rs	pub(crate)	E	(&self, names: &std::collections::BTreeSet<String>) -> std::collections::BTreeSet<String>	FAIL	RET=TEXT(String); RET=UNKNOWN(std::collections::BTreeSet<String>)	names
DK1	scoped_key_at_or_above	lexscope/walk.rs	-	E	(&self, prefix: &crate::ScopeRef, name: &str, hit: impl Fn(&AtKey) -> bool) -> Option<DeclKey>	FAIL	CB:hit=CB(a callback Fn(&AtKey)); CB:hit.0=UNKNOWN(AtKey); RET=CARD(Option in Option<DeclKey>); RET=UNKNOWN(DeclKey)	prefix,name
